            <ArticleTitle>Social health and the forgiving heart: the Type B story.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evolution of the Type A hypothesis is well documented. The protective corresponding Type B construct has not evolved similarly. Using experiences from Friedman's Recurrent Coronary Prevention Project, on a speculative basis, four neglected protective processes are examined: uniqueness/self-esteem/autonomy, forgiveness, sociability, and &quot;causal&quot; wisdom attributions. A more integrative set of questions is proposed to expand our knowledge of adaptive fitness and success.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
